  "notes": "Astra Agro Lestari (AALI) — IDX-listed Indonesian palm oil producer, subsidiary of Astra International. ~213,000 ha planted area (~287k ha total concessions), ~527k acres total. Reports under PSAK (IFRS-equivalent); biological assets carried at fair value under PSAK 69. Quarterly + FY filings via IDX (laporan keuangan). Values in IDR millions (matches seed-comps.json convention). Acres derived from planted-ha × 2.47 = thousand acres; planted area grew from ~80k ha (1998 IPO) to ~213k ha (2024). Quarterly revenue/segment splits from interim financial statements; FY data from audited annual reports. Segments: CPO (~85% rev), PK (~7%), Soybean / olive products / other plantations (residual). FV adjustment on biological assets appears in expensesBySegmentMM where disclosed. Net debt swung negative (cash > debt) post 2022 CPO boom, returned to mild positive in 2023-2024. Pre-2010 periods are annual only — quarterly archives sparse pre-2010. 1998-2010 sourced from AALI annual report 5-year-summary tables and historical IDX filings.",
